85	746,577,1198,1448	Fig. 85.	A Lily of the Valley leaf, long and pointed, its many fine nerves running side by side without branching from the base to the point.
86	1295,587,1724,1444	86. Parallel-veined Leaves	A Calla leaf, broad and arrow-based on its stalk, with a stout midrib from which close parallel veins run out to the margins.
